{=============================================================================
{Variant: runnable variant of the blocked native file (see README.md, conversion log). Changes, all forced by a CoolSolve gap and logged there: (1) the variables K|star_r_n and K|star_r of the original are renamed Kstar_r_n and Kstar_r (CS-GAP-NAME-PIPE); (2) the four CALL BRINEPROP(...) library calls are replaced by the four brine properties stored by EES for the default operating point (CS-GAP-INCLUDE / CS-GAP-LKT); (3) the five EES 5-argument IF(A,B,X,Y,Z) calls are replaced by the 3-argument CoolSolve if(A-B,X,Z) form (CS-GAP-IF5); (4) the string output WetHumide$, written with the EES intrinsic IF$ in the original, is removed: CoolSolve does not implement IF$ and the string feeds no equation. No other equation, name or value changes.}
  Cooling coil RefSim model (dry and wet regimes, one zone)
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0074
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The cooling coil is treated as a one-zone counter-flow heat exchanger. The
  fully dry and the fully wet regimes are described simultaneously and the
  regime to be considered is the one leading to the maximal cooling coil
  capacity (Braun et al., 1989). The heat transfer coefficient AU is
  calculated by considering three resistances in series: the convective
  resistance on the air side, the conduction resistance of the metal and the
  convective resistance on the refrigerant side. When the coil works in the
  wet regime, the air is replaced by a fictitious perfect gas, whose enthalpy
  is fully defined by the actual wet bulb temperature (Lebrun et al., 1990).
  To determine the air state at the coil outlet in the wet regime, a
  fictitious semi-isothermal heat exchanger is defined, according to the ASHRAE
  classical procedure (ASHRAE 2000). One of the two fluids supplying this
  exchanger is the air; the other one is a fictitious fluid of infinite
  capacity flow rate, whose uniform temperature is supposed to correspond to
  the average temperature of the external surface of the coil, also called
  contact temperature.

  The refrigerant side is a secondary refrigerant (ethylene glycol or
  propylene glycol solution) whose properties are given by the BrineProp
  library procedure of the laboratory, called here with CALL.

  Inputs : t_a_su_coil, RH_su_coil, P_atm, M_dot_a_coil, M_dot_r_coil,
           t_r_su_coil (supply air and refrigerant, diagram window),
           R_a_coil_n, R_m_coil, R_r_coil_n, M_dot_a_coil_n, M_dot_r_coil_n,
           conc_r, K|star_r_n (parameters, diagram window)
  Outputs: Q_dot_coil, Q_dot_sens_coil, Q_dot_lat_coil, t_a_ex_coil,
           t_wb_ex_coil, M_dot_w_coil, t_r_ex_coil, SHR, WetHumide$
  Units  : SI - temperatures in °C, pressures in Pa, energies in J
  Source : ULiège model bank (Laborelec toolkit lineage), cooling coil RefSim
           model, 18 March 2008, V. Lemort and J. Lebrun - see README.md
=============================================================================}

"!Nomenclature (as in the original)"
"AU           Global heat transfer coefficient [W/K]"
"C_dot        Capacity flow rate [W/K]"
"conc_r       Concentration of propylene or ethylene glycol [%]"
"c_p          Specific heat [J/kg-K]"
"h            Specific enthalpy [J/kg]"
"Kstar       Thermal properties coefficient [(m.s)^(m-1).J/kg^m/K]"
"M_dot        Mass flow rate [kg/s]"
"NTU          Number of transfer units [-]"
"p            Pressure [Pa]"
"Q_dot        Thermal power [W]"
"R            Thermal resistance [K/W]"
"refrigerant  Nature of the refrigerant (string variable)"
"RH           Relative humidity [-]"
"SHR          Sensible heat ratio [-]"
"t            Temperature [°C]"
"v            Specific volume [m^3/kg]"
"W            Specific humidity [kg water/kg dry air]"
"DELTAt       Temperature difference [K]"
"epsilon      Efficiency [-]"
"mu           Dynamic viscosity [Pa.s]"
"omega        Capacity flow rate ratio [-]"
"rho          Density [kg/m^3]"

"!References (as in the original)"
"[1] ASHRAE. 2000. 2000 ASHRAE handbook-HVAC Systems and Equipment, Chapter 21. Atlanta: American Society of Heating, Refrigerating and Air-Conditioning Engineers, Inc."
"[2] Braun, J.E., S.A. Klein, and J. Mitchell. 1989. Effectiveness Models for Cooling Towers and Cooling Coils. ASHRAE Transaction 95(2):164-173."
"[3] Incropera, F., P., D., P., DeWitt (2002) Fundamentals of Heat and Mass Transfer, Fifth Edition, John Wiley & Sons"
"[4] Lebrun, J., X. Ding, J.-P. Eppe, and M. Wasacz. 1990. Cooling Coil Models to be used in Transient and/or Wet Regimes. Theoretical Analysis and Experimental Validation. Proceedings of SSB 1990. Liège:405-441."

"!Disclaimer of the original: the accuracy or reliability of the information is not guaranteed or warranted in any way; the model is freely distributed and may not be sold or distributed for commercial purpose; the user is asked to cite his sources and the origin of the model."

"!1. INPUTS (entered in the diagram window of the original)"
t_a_su_coil = 30        "supply air dry bulb temperature [°C]"
RH_su_coil = 0.5        "supply air relative humidity [-]"
P_atm = 98000           "atmospheric pressure [Pa] (value stored by EES)"
M_dot_a_coil = 1.8      "air mass flow rate [kg/s]"
M_dot_r_coil = 1.7      "refrigerant mass flow rate [kg/s]"
t_r_su_coil = 6         "refrigerant supply temperature [°C]"

"!2. PARAMETERS (entered in the diagram window of the original)"
Kstar_r_n = 106         "nominal thermal properties coefficient [(m.s)^(m-1).J/kg^m/K]"
refrigerant$ = 'EG'     "nature of the secondary refrigerant: 'EG' or 'PG'"
conc_r = 35             "concentration of the secondary refrigerant [%]"
R_a_coil_n = 0.0001319  "nominal air-side thermal resistance [K/W]"
R_r_coil_n = 0.0001199  "nominal refrigerant-side thermal resistance [K/W]"
R_m_coil = 6.596E-06    "thermal resistance of the metal [K/W]"
M_dot_a_coil_n = 1.803  "nominal air mass flow rate [kg/s]"
M_dot_r_coil_n = 1.866  "nominal refrigerant mass flow rate [kg/s]"

"!3. OUTPUTS (commented out in the original, listed here for reference)"
"Q_dot_coil       cooling coil total capacity [W]"
"Q_dot_sens_coil  cooling coil sensible capacity [W]"
"Q_dot_lat_coil   cooling coil latent capacity [W]"
"t_r_ex_coil      temperature of the refrigerant at the exhaust of the coil [°C]"
"t_a_ex_coil      dry bulb temperature of the air at the exhaust of the coil [°C]"
"t_wb_ex_coil     wet bulb temperature of the air at the exhaust of the coil [°C]"
"M_dot_w_coil     condensate flow rate [kg/s]"

"!4. EQUATIONS"

"4.1. Supply status"
t_wb_su_coil = wetbulb(AIRH2O,T=t_a_su_coil,P=P_atm,R=RH_su_coil)
t_dp_su_coil = dewpoint(AIRH2O,T=t_a_su_coil,P=P_atm,w=W_su_coil)
h_a_su_coil = enthalpy(AIRH2O,T=t_a_su_coil,P=P_atm,R = RH_su_coil)
c_p_a_coil = specheat(AIRH2O,T=t_a_su_coil,P=P_atm,R=RH_su_coil)
W_su_coil = humrat(AIRH2O,T=t_a_su_coil,P=P_atm,R=RH_su_coil)
v_a_su_coil = volume(AIRH2O,T=t_a_su_coil,P=P_atm,R=RH_su_coil)

"4.2. Definition of thermal resistances:"
R_a_coil = R_a_coil_n*(M_dot_a_coil_n / M_dot_a_coil)^0.6  "laminar flow between flat plates"
R_r_coil = R_r_coil_n*Kstar_r_n/Kstar_r*(M_dot_r_coil_n / M_dot_r_coil)^0.8  "turbulent flow in circular tube"
m = 0.8   "exponent in the Dittus Boelter relationship, giving the Nusselt number as a function of Reynolds and Prandtl numbers (Incropera and DeWitt, 2002)"
n = 0.3   "idem"
Kstar_r = mu_r_coil^(n-m)*k_r_coil^(1-n)*c_p_r_coil^n  "variation of refrigerant side resistance with refrigerant properties"
rho_r_coil = 1051.354719      "BrineProp 'Density' of the secondary refrigerant [kg/m^3]"
c_p_r_coil = 3576.11699        "BrineProp 'SpecHeat' of the secondary refrigerant [J/kg-K]"
mu_r_coil = 0.003951911085    "BrineProp 'DynVisc' of the secondary refrigerant [Pa.s]"
k_r_coil = 0.4326901231       "BrineProp 'thermalc' of the secondary refrigerant [W/m-K]"

"4.3. Dry regime description"

"4.3.1. Capacity in dry regime"
1/AU_coil_dry = R_a_coil + R_m_coil + R_r_coil
NTU_coil_dry = AU_coil_dry / C_dot_min_coil_dry
epsilon_coil_dry*(1 - omega_coil_dry*exp(-NTU_coil_dry*(1 - omega_coil_dry))) = (1 - exp(-NTU_coil_dry*(1 - omega_coil_dry)))
Q_dot_coil_dry = epsilon_coil_dry*C_dot_min_coil_dry*(t_a_su_coil - t_r_su_coil)
C_dot_min_coil_dry = min(C_dot_a_coil, C_dot_r_coil)
omega_coil_dry = C_dot_min_coil_dry / C_dot_max_coil_dry
C_dot_max_coil_dry = max(C_dot_a_coil, C_dot_r_coil)

"4.3.2. Air side"
C_dot_a_coil = M_dot_a_coil*c_p_a_coil
Q_dot_coil_dry = C_dot_a_coil*(t_a_su_coil - t_a_ex_coil_dry)
W_ex_coil_dry = W_su_coil
t_dp_ex_coil_dry = dewpoint(AIRH2O,T=t_a_ex_coil_dry,P=P_atm,w=W_ex_coil_dry)
(t_c_ex_coil_dry - t_r_su_coil)/(R_r_coil + R_m_coil) = (t_a_ex_coil_dry - t_r_su_coil)/(R_a_coil + R_m_coil + R_r_coil)
DELTA_t_cond = t_dp_ex_coil_dry - t_c_ex_coil_dry  "condensation may occur only if this term is positive"

"4.3.2. Refrigerant side"
C_dot_r_coil = M_dot_r_coil*c_p_r_coil

"4.4. Wet regime description"

"4.4.1. Capacity in wet regime"
R_af_coil = R_a_coil*c_p_a_coil / c_p_af_coil
1/AU_coil_wet = R_af_coil + R_m_coil + R_r_coil
NTU_coil_wet = AU_coil_wet / C_dot_min_coil_wet
C_dot_max_coil_wet = max(C_dot_af_coil, C_dot_r_coil)
C_dot_min_coil_wet = min(C_dot_af_coil, C_dot_r_coil)
omega_coil_wet = C_dot_min_coil_wet / C_dot_max_coil_wet
epsilon_coil_wet*(1 - omega_coil_wet*exp(-NTU_coil_wet*(1 - omega_coil_wet))) = (1 - exp(-NTU_coil_wet*(1 - omega_coil_wet)))
Q_dot_coil_wet = epsilon_coil_wet*C_dot_min_coil_wet*(t_wb_su_coil - t_r_su_coil)

"4.4.2. Air side:"

"4.4.2.1. Capacity"
Q_dot_coil_wet = M_dot_a_coil*((h_a_su_coil - h_a_ex_coil_wet) - (W_su_coil - W_ex_coil_wet)*c_w_coil*t_w_coil)

"4.4.2.2. Definition of fictitious air"
Q_dot_coil_wet = C_dot_af_coil*(t_wb_su_coil - t_wb_ex_coil_wet)
C_dot_af_coil = M_dot_a_coil*c_p_af_coil  "according to Merckel theory and assuming that Lewis = 1"

"4.4.2.3. Calculation of exhaust state"
h_a_su_coil - h_a_ex_coil_wet = epsilon_c_coil_wet*(h_a_su_coil - h_c_coil_wet)  "fictitious isothermal contact surface:"
W_su_coil - W_ex_coil_wet = epsilon_c_coil_wet*(W_su_coil - W_c_coil_wet)  "to calculate W_ex_coil_wet"
epsilon_c_coil_wet = 1 - exp(-NTU_c_coil_wet)  "contact effectiveness"
NTU_c_coil_wet = 1/(R_a_coil*C_dot_a_coil)
h_a_ex_coil_wet = enthalpy(AIRH2O,T=t_a_ex_coil_wet,P=P_atm,R = RH_ex_coil_wet)
W_ex_coil_wet = humrat(AIRH2O,T=t_a_ex_coil_wet,P=P_atm,R = RH_ex_coil_wet)
t_wb_ex_coil_wet = wetbulb(AIRH2O,T=t_a_ex_coil_wet,P=P_atm,w=W_ex_coil_wet)
h_c_coil_wet = enthalpy(AIRH2O,T=t_c_coil_wet,P=P_atm,R = 1)
W_c_coil_wet = humrat(AIRH2O,T=t_c_coil_wet,P=P_atm,R = 1)
M_dot_w_coil_wet = M_dot_a_coil*(W_su_coil - W_ex_coil_wet)

"4.4.2.4. Condensate properties:"
c_w_coil = 4187  "specific heat of the condensate [J/kg-K]"
t_w_coil = t_c_coil_wet  "temperature of the condensate [°C]"

"4.5. Cooling coil capacity"

"4.5.1. Total cooling capacity"
Q_dot_coil = if(Q_dot_coil_wet-Q_dot_coil_dry, Q_dot_coil_wet,Q_dot_coil_dry)
Q_dot_sens_coil = C_dot_a_coil*(t_a_su_coil-t_a_ex_coil)
Q_dot_lat_coil = Q_dot_coil-Q_dot_sens_coil

"4.6. Global heat transfer coefficient"
AU_coil = if(Q_dot_coil_wet-Q_dot_coil_dry,AU_coil_wet,AU_coil_dry)

"4.5.2. Condensate flow rate:"
M_dot_w_coil = if(Q_dot_coil_wet-Q_dot_coil_dry,M_dot_w_coil_wet,0)

"4.6. Exhaust air state:"
t_a_ex_coil = if(Q_dot_coil_wet-Q_dot_coil_dry,t_a_ex_coil_wet,t_a_ex_coil_dry)
W_ex_coil = if(Q_dot_coil_wet-Q_dot_coil_dry,W_ex_coil_wet,W_ex_coil_dry)
RH_ex_coil = relhum(AIRH2O,T=t_a_ex_coil,P=P_atm,w=W_ex_coil)
v_a_ex_coil = volume(AIRH2O,T=t_a_ex_coil,P=P_atm,w=W_ex_coil)

"4.7. Exhaust refrigerant state"
Q_dot_coil = C_dot_r_coil*(t_r_ex_coil-t_r_su_coil)

"SHR"
SHR = Q_dot_sens_coil/Q_dot_coil
